**Current support versus accepted design.** The Alpha compiler accepts parenthesised grouped `project` and `html` records and declaration-owned `#Config of T` inputs. Closed `$project` / `$html_builder` configuration, the required `version` argument and `$config` prefixes remain accepted queued design. The module diagnostic limit below now governs ordinary-body diagnostic recovery. The project diagnostic threshold is accepted and validated but is not yet applied, so project scheduling effects arrive in a later phase. `moth new` does not yet emit the starter below. See @../progress (Progress) and @../directives (Directives).

`config.moth` is the single project config file. It lives at the project root, is loaded before source-tree discovery and is one self-contained compile-time source file with no source dependencies, package resolution or authored file-value paths.

### Accepted project config

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    $config
    version #String = "0.1.0"

    $project(
        name = "my_site",
        version = version,
        entry_root = "src",
    )

    $html_builder
]

A fixed literal version also works. A contract named `version` does not satisfy an omitted `$project` argument. A project field named `version` does not satisfy a source input contract.

The required generated starter, once implementation lands, keeps the same version contract and explicit `version = version` argument. It may also pass retained scaffold fields such as `author`, `license` and selected HTML defaults. Do not treat `"0.1.0"` as a `$project` default.

### The `$project` directive

`config.moth` contains exactly one `$project` invocation. The positional order is:

[table:
    [th:
        [: Parameter]
        [: Type]
        [: Default]
        [: Configurable value permitted]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `name`]
        [: `String`]
        [: Required]
        [: No]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `version`]
        [: `String`]
        [: Required]
        [: Yes]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `entry_root`]
        [: `String`]
        [: `"src"`]
        [: No]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `author`]
        [: `String?`]
        [: `none`]
        [: Yes]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `license`]
        [: `String?`]
        [: `none`]
        [: Yes]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `template_const_loop_iteration_limit`]
        [: `I32`]
        [: The existing compiler-owned default]
        [: No]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `max_errors_per_module`]
        [: `I32?`]
        [: `5`]
        [: No]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `max_errors_per_project`]
        [: `I32?`]
        [: `30`]
        [: No]
    ]
]

The signature is closed. Arbitrary fields, misspelled standard fields and `metadata = ...` are rejected. `@project` publishes only the first six predefined fields. The two diagnostic limits are compiler controls and are never published.

`name`, `entry_root`, `template_const_loop_iteration_limit`, `max_errors_per_module` and `max_errors_per_project` remain fixed-only, including through helper constants. Missing `version` is diagnosed even when an unused input contract named `version` exists.

### Diagnostic limits

`max_errors_per_module` is a strict allowance of primary errors retained for each module. It bounds ordinary-body diagnostic recovery. After the first failed ordinary body the emitter admits a further eligible body only while the retained primary error count stays below the allowance.

`max_errors_per_project` is an accepted soft scheduling threshold for the whole command. It is validated and stored but is not yet applied, so it does not stop compilation work today. Once applied, work already running will finish and keep its errors, and the project total may therefore exceed the threshold. It is not a maximum result count.

A present value must be an `I32` from 1 to 2147483647. Zero, negative values and other types are rejected. Omitting a setting uses its default. An explicit `none` disables that one count and leaves the other unchanged. Warnings, notes and related labels never count. Neither setting disables the compiler's fixed recovery-work guard or changes program meaning.

### `$html_builder`

An authored HTML directory project contains exactly one `$html_builder` invocation. Bare `$html_builder` uses defaults. `$html_builder()` is invalid. The command selects the builder first; this directive never selects a backend or platform.

The positional order and defaults are:

[table:
    [th:
        [: Parameter]
        [: Type]
        [: Default]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `dev_output`]
        [: `String`]
        [: `"dev"`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `release_output`]
        [: `String`]
        [: `"release"`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `origin`]
        [: `String`]
        [: `"/"`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `page_url_style`]
        [: `String`]
        [: `"trailing_slash"`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `redirect_index_html`]
        [: `Bool`]
        [: `true`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `html_lang`]
        [: `String`]
        [: `"en"`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `html_title_prefix`]
        [: `String`]
        [: `""`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `html_title_postfix`]
        [: `String`]
        [: `""`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `html_favicon`]
        [: `String?`]
        [: `none`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `html_inject_charset`]
        [: `Bool`]
        [: `true`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `html_inject_viewport`]
        [: `Bool`]
        [: `true`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `html_inject_color_scheme`]
        [: `Bool`]
        [: `true`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `html_inject_core_css`]
        [: `Bool`]
        [: `true`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `html_body_style`]
        [: `String`]
        [: `""`]
    ]
]

`page_url_style` accepts `trailing_slash`, `no_trailing_slash` or `ignore`. `html_favicon` accepts a compile-time String containing an untracked URL, not necessarily a string literal. Tracked file resources belong in `$page` metadata because `config.moth` rejects authored file-value paths.

Unknown or inactive unsupported directives error. Multi-builder configuration waits for `$feature`. Synthetic single-file operations without authored `config.moth` keep their explicit synthetic path and do not invent `$project` / `$html_builder` source.

### Current grouped config

Operational config uses declaration-owned `#Config` inputs and parenthesised grouped records:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    version #Config of String = "0.1.0"
    project_error_limit #I32? = none

    project #= (
        name = "moth_docs",
        version = version,
        entry_root = "src",
        max_errors_per_module = 5,
        max_errors_per_project = project_error_limit,
    )

    html #= (
        dev_output = "dev",
        release_output = "release",
    )
]

The grouped `project` record accepts `max_errors_per_module` and `max_errors_per_project` as fixed-only `I32?` compiler controls. Omission uses the default of 5 module errors or 30 project errors. An explicit `none` disables that one limit and leaves the other unchanged. A present value must be an exact `I32` from 1 to 2147483647. The grouped record has no field type context, so write an explicit absence through a typed `I32?` constant as the example does. Writing `none` directly in the record is a language type error. The loader validates and stores both settings today. The module limit now governs ordinary-body diagnostic recovery. The project threshold is accepted but not yet applied, so scheduling behaviour is unchanged until a later phase.

Retired flat keys remain rejected. Keep live `docs/config.moth` on this current path.

### Concepts related to project config

- For `$config` input contracts see @#build-inputs (Build configuration values).
- For `$page` see @#entry-config (Entry metadata and page directives).
- For general directive grammar see @../directives (Directives).
